cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Types Without Taxa: analysis code for a matched-null test of whether the
  clusters a pipeline reports are real
message: "If you use this code, please cite the accompanying paper and this archive."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Miura
    family-names: Meng
    email: meng10@upenn.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1522-1997"
    affiliation: "University of Pennsylvania"
repository-code: "https://github.com/haomeng797-ship-it/types-without-taxa"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and preregistered materials for a matched-null test of
  cluster-count claims, applied to three large public personality datasets.
  A synthetic null population is built to share the real data's marginal
  distributions and full correlation structure while containing no latent types
  by construction; the number of clusters a pipeline reports on the real data is
  then compared with what the same pipeline reports on the null. Includes the
  specification curve across all fourteen mclust covariance parameterizations,
  positive controls, taxometric analyses, and the figures reported in the paper.
keywords:
  - clustering
  - copula
  - null model
  - mixture models
  - personality
  - psychometrics
  - taxometrics
  - preregistration
  - R
